  "description": "Captures a self issued by a bureaucracy. An epidemic of sudden, permanent amnesia leaves the unclaimed amnesiacs to a state programme that rebuilds their identities from cassette-tape instructions: ride a bike, eat an apple, jump from a height, record it all on Polaroids. Nikou's deadpan Greek dystopia is about what a person is when their past arrives as a form to complete — memory as paperwork, completed diligently.\n\nAmidst a worldwide pandemic that causes sudden amnesia, middle-aged Aris finds himself enrolled in a recovery program designed to help unclaimed patients build new identities.",
